load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# A Coxeter group: a group generated by reflections, each generator squaring to the identity, with the only further
# relations fixing the angle between each pair of mirrors. Coxeter groups are the symmetry groups of regular polytopes
# and the reflection groups that tile spaces. The reflections in the faces of the 24-cell generate the infinite Coxeter
# group of the {3,4,3,4} honeycomb, which is exactly how one cell, reflected endlessly like a mirror, tiles the whole
# hyperbolic four-space of the mesh. The form carries the generating reflections; the involution and angle relations are
# the defining laws.
form coxeter-group
  link generators, like set
